       The  ggeetteennttrrooppyy()  function  writes _l_e_n_g_t_h bytes of high‐quality random
       data to the buffer starting at the location pointed to by _b_u_f_f_e_r.   The
       maximum permitted value for the _l_e_n_g_t_h argument is 256.

       A  successful call to ggeetteennttrrooppyy() always provides the requested number
       of bytes of entropy.

